  "jlptLevel": "N5",
  "category": "adjectives",
  "explanation": {
    "en": "The negative form of い-adjectives is used to say something is not true. To make the negative, change the final い to くない.\n\nKey points:\n• い-adjective negative: い → くない\n• Add です for politeness: 高くないです\n• Used for present/future negative\n• Same pattern for all い-adjectives\n\nFor example, “高い” becomes “高くない” (not expensive). “暑い” becomes “暑くない” (not hot).\n\nYou can say “この店は高くないです” to mean “This shop is not expensive.”\n\nRemember: you do not use ではありません with い-adjectives. Use くない instead.\n\nPractice with common adjectives: 安い → 安くない, おいしい → おいしくない, 大きい → 大きくない.",
    "ja": ""
  },
  "structure": {
    "pattern": "i-adjective (negative) + です",
    "components": [
      {
        "part": "i-adjective (negative)",
        "explanation": "Change い → くない",
        "examples": ["高くない", "暑くない", "おいしくない"]
      },
      {
        "part": "です",
        "explanation": "Polite ending (optional)",
        "examples": ["です"]
      }
    ]
  },
